                            <table class="table table-bordered" width="80%" align="center" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
                                        <tbody><tr><td class="subheader class14">Liquidity Position</td></tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="class11">
                                                        <b> Adequate </b>
                                        </td>
                                    </tr>
                                                                    <tr>
                                        <td class="class11">
                                            <div style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12px"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'">­Acuite believes that IREDA will maintain adequate liquidity profile as it has sufficient long-term banking credit lines and unutilized credit lines and has cash and cash equivalents &amp; bank balances of Rs 717.15 Cr. as on March 31, 2026. As per the ALM statement dated March 31, 2026, IREDA’s repayment obligations during FY2026-27 are expected to be Rs. 16,087.34 Cr., against receivables of around Rs. 16,575.26 Cr. over the same period, resulting in an expected cumulative positive mismatch of Rs. 487.92 Cr over this period.&nbsp;Acuite considers the financial flexibility available due to GoI ownership and undrawn sanctioned bank lines.</span></span><br>
<br>
&nbsp;</div>

                                        </td>
